  "source_observation_note": "The official eLife article was inspected from its indexed full-text result, including its title, single-cell circadian-neuron scope, 17 clock-neuron categories, figure description for 2,615 cells, LD/DD framing, and data-availability link to GSE157504 and the Rosbash lab analysis repository. Direct GEO page access returned a CAPTCHA and the direct eLife page request returned 403 in this session; the GEO search result still exposed GSE157504 and a CT02 sample, and the official eLife supplementary XLSX was downloaded from the eLife CDN and hash-checked.",
  "analysis_context": {
    "time_system": "LD samples are reported as ZT; DD samples are reported as CT. The author annotation stores a ztNN token in some DD cell IDs, so the join applies a condition-aware zt-to-CT alias without relabeling the experimental condition.",
    "experimental_unit": "The single-cell columns are observations nested within source experiment/collection replicate; they are not independent fly-level replicates. The raw-count output is descriptive only.",
    "normalization_status": "Raw matrix outputs are UMI counts with no normalization or rhythm model. The separate supplement extraction transcribes author-reported TP10K-based high-confidence cycling calls and does not re-fit them.",
    "biological_unit_limitations": "The paper reports two experiments per condition. The supplied cell annotation does not identify individual flies or establish the fly-pool size per collection in the files reviewed. The source rhythmicity methods used individual cells as JTK replicates and randomly split cells for Fourier analysis; uncertainty is not re-estimated at biological-experiment level here. No channel protein, current, voltage, or causal behavior conclusion is supported by this transcript-only audit."
  },
